IDEAS

This folder keeps the ideas we find in other shells: what they do well
that tam-clam should learn from, and what they do badly that tam-clam
should avoid.


ONE FILE PER SHELL

  <name>.md, for example bash.md or fish.md. Each file has:

    What it is           language, license, size, scope
    Ideas worth taking   each with a verdict and a reason
    Things to avoid      each with a reason
    Where to look        files or docs to read when we act on an idea

  Verdicts:

    adopt     we want this; it has (or will get) a place in a plan
    consider  promising; needs a closer look or Fred's view
    reject    we decided against it, and the reason says why

  An idea that tam-clam builds gets the plan or version that delivered it,
  for example "adopt (P1, 0.0.1)". When code is taken, not just the idea,
  it is also recorded in UPSTREAM.md.

  synthesis.md gathers the best ideas from every file by topic, and is the
  place to start.


REFERENCE CLONES

  sources lists the shells we keep a local clone of, so we can read their
  code and follow their fixes. tools/pull-references brings every listed
  clone up to date and clones any that are missing:

    tools/pull-references          pull every listed clone
    tools/pull-references --list   show what is listed and where

  The clones live outside this repository (under ~/Code). Nothing is ever
  pushed or posted to those projects.


HOW DEEP THESE NOTES GO

  bash, dash, zsh, fish, mksh, Oils and busybox ash were read from source
  on 2026-11-17 (commits in UPSTREAM.md). The others (ksh93, yash, rc, es,
  elvish, nushell, xonsh, PowerShell, tcsh) are starter notes from the
  projects' known designs, marked as such, to be checked against source
  before we act on them. A full "survey the field" happens only when
  Fred asks for one.
